 blends earnest, confessional voiceover and melodramatic plotting with quieter, character-focused moments; thematically it explores coming-of-age, identity, love, loyalty, and grief. The tone is at once sentimental and introspective, often foregrounding emotional dialogue and relationship-driven conflict, and the show helped define late-1990s/early-2000s network teen drama sensibilities.", "external": {"facebook": {"id": "dawsonscreek"}, "imdb": {"id": "tt0118300", "user_rating": 6.8, "user_rating_count": 49286}, "wikidata": {"id": "q461357"}}, "filming_location": "University of North Carolina Wilmington - 601 South College Road, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Airlie Gardens - 300 Airlie Road, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, 6401 Pine Grove Drive, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Cape Cod, Massachusetts, USA, Dock Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, 111 Ann Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Airlie Road, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Holiday Inn Sunspree Resort - 1706 N. Lumina Avenue, Wrightsville Beach, North Carolina, USA, Elijah's Restaurant - 2 Ann Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, USS North Carolina Battleship Memorial Park - 1 Battleship Road NE, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Alton Lennon Federal Building and Courthouse - 2 Princess Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Duke University, Durham, North Carolina, USA, Franklin Street, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA, South Carolina, USA, Southport, North Carolina, USA, Wrightsville Beach, North Carolina, USA, Head Road, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, Dockside Restaurant and Bar - 1308 Airlie Road, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, 207 S 3rd Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, 115 S Water Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, EUE/Screen Gems Studios - 1223 N 23rd Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, 5 S Water Street, Wilmington, North Carolina, USA, 4 Marina Street, Wrightsville Beach, North Carolina, USA, CD Alley Music - 8 Market Stree